# Runtime state — never tracked. The event log is sacred state and belongs to
# the instance, not the source repository.
#
# NOTE: these are anchored with a leading slash so they match only at the
# repository root. An unanchored pattern like `postgres/` matches a directory
# of that name ANYWHERE in the tree — which silently excluded
# src/adapters/postgres/ on the first attempt. Keep them anchored.
/state/
/config/instance.json
*.jsonl
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
/memory-graph.json
/conversation.json
/self-model.json
/soul.json
/captured-functions/
/event-log/

# Secrets and credentials
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
key.txt
bot.txt
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

# Build output
*.fasl
*.fas
*.lib
*.dx32fsl
*.dx64fsl
/build/
/dist/
/.tools/
/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/pai
/pai.exe

# Embedded service data (standalone mode) — anchored, see note above
/postgres/
/ollama/
/logs/
/artifacts/curiosity-lab/
/artifacts/context-graph-lab/
/artifacts/context-graph-calibration/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
\#*\#
.\#*
.clone-state/
/.claude/
/.cache/
/.q5-lifecycle-state/
/.pai-review/
/.scratch/
/.pai-promotion-backups/
/.pai-promotion-staging/
/.uv-cache/
/runtime-backups/
/.publication-output/
/.test-logs/

CodexAssessment*.md
docs/multi-instance-fleet-design.md
